    "created_at": "2020-01-10T21:18:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-01-10T21:18:32Z",
    "body": "Actually, `sup` and `sub` *are* tagged this way. I'm guessing the scraper guesses element definitions if the `dfn` is in a *heading* with an id of the form \"the-foo-element\", but it doesn't apply that heuristic to the `dfn`'s id itself.\r\n\r\nSo any heading that contains more than one element dfn won't trigger the heuristic, and needs its dfns correctly tagged. (h1-6 and sup/sub are the only elements defined with this pattern.)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
